-- let_forward_reference at 11:13: the same rule one hop away (`language.md`
-- §7). `a`'s initialiser does not name `b` at all; it names `f`, and naming a
-- `let` function may call it — `List.map` would — so `f`'s body reads `b`
-- before `b` has a value. The region is the mention of `f`, because that is
-- the reference that runs too soon, and the message names `b` and its line.
-- `later` is the legal shape: it calls the same `f` from BELOW `b`, where
-- `b` is initialised.
g =
    a = f 1
    f x = x + b
    b = 2
    later = f 10
    a + later
